SUMMARY:The Speaker's Series: The Astonishing Lives of Older Women
DESCRIPTION:Ontario Speaker Donna Skelly welcomes author and Toronto Star journalist Moira Welsh to Queen’s Park for the next installment of The Speaker’s Series on Monday\, April 20 from 6:00 to 7:00 p.m. The event will explore the financial challenges facing older women\, drawing on Welsh’s new book\, The Astonishing Lives of Older Women. \nThe Speaker’s Series invites attendees to experience Ontario’s rich and diverse history through a collection of engaging\, in-person talks that celebrate the people\, places\, and moments that shape our province. \nThis event is free to the public. Register online at the Legislative Assembly of Ontario’s website.  \nVisitors 16 years of age and older must present a piece of government-issued photo ID to enter the building. All visitors must pass through an airport-style security screening to enter the Legislative Building. Please arrive by 5:30 p.m. to guarantee seating and timely access through security. 
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/the-speakers-series-the-astonishing-lives-of-older-women/
LOCATION:Legislative Assembly of Ontario\, 111 Wellesley St W\, Toronto\, ON M7A 1A2\, Canada\, Old Toronto\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M7A 1A2
CATEGORIES:Talks & Panels
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/the-speakers-series-the-astonishing-lives-of-older-women.png
END:VEVENT
