SUMMARY:Limited Edition: A History of Violence
DESCRIPTION:In this stylized thriller from director David Cronenberg\, Viggo Mortensen stars as Tom McKenna\, a well-respected man who leads a quiet\, charmed life with his loving wife and family in a small town. But when he kills a robber in self-defense at the diner he runs\, Tom is lauded by the national media as a vigilante hero. Unfortunately\, the media spotlight also brings him to the attention of some sleazy criminals who recognize Tom as a former associate gone underground. Now\, to protect his family from certain peril\, Tom must return to his secret past and confront A History of Violence. \nWorking with an exceptional cast that also includes Maria Bello\, Ed Harris\, and William Hurt\, Cronenberg slyly deconstructs the mythos of the American action hero\, posing elemental questions about identity\, human nature\, and the violence that we both abhor and can’t look away from.
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/limited-edition-a-history-of-violence/
LOCATION:2236 Queen Street East\, 2236 Queen St E\, Toronto\, ON M4E 1G2\, Canada\, Old Toronto\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M4E 1G2
CATEGORIES:Film & Media
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/limited-edition-a-history-of-violence.png
END:VEVENT
